    "result_text": "The full suite passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` + the owner's id. I implemented it with minimal structural impact by touching only two files and no large classes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a `selfLink` read-only string property on the `Owner` response schema (the generated `OwnerDto` picks it up from here).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` expression to the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(\\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")\n   ```\n\n`OwnerMapper` is a MapStruct interface whose methods each have trivial cyclomatic complexity, so the surrounding-context cost (`WMC_other`) is tiny \u2014 far cheaper than adding a getter to the large `Owner` entity or editing the busy `OwnerRestControllerV1.getOwner`. The new mapping is a one-line, CC-1 addition, and no method was grown in complexity.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink` passes, and the full `mvn test` build is green.",
